„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ»Because Manasseh king of Judah hath done these abominations, and hath done wickedly above all that the Amorites did, which were before him, and hath made Judah also to sin with his idols:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ therefore thus saith the LORD God of Israel, Behold, I am bringing such evil upon Jerusalem and Judah, that whosoever heareth of it, both his ears shall tingle.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙµAnd I will stretch over Jerusalem the line of Samaria, and the plummet of the house of Ahab: and I will wipe Jerusalem as a man wipeth a dish, wiping it, and turning it upside down.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ£And I will forsake the remnant of mine inheritance, and deliver them into the hand of their enemies; and they shall become a prey and a spoil to all their enemies;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŸbecause they have done that which was evil in my sight, and have provoked me to anger, since the day their fathers came forth out of Egypt, even unto this day.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÌMoreover Manasseh shed innocent blood very much, till he had filled Jerusalem from one end to another; beside his sin wherewith he made Judah to sin, in doing that which was evil in the sight of the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ Now the rest of the acts of Manasseh, and all that he did, and his sin that he sinned, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘And Manasseh slept with his fathers, and was buried in the garden of his own house, in the garden of Uzza: and Amon his son reigned in his stead.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ©Amon was twenty and two years old when he began to reign, and he reigned two years in Jerusalem. And his mother's name was Meshullemeth, the daughter of Haruz of Jotbah.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTAnd he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD, as his father Manasseh did.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyAnd he walked in all the way that his father walked in, and served the idols that his father served, and worshipped them:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙRand he forsook the LORD God of his fathers, and walked not in the way of the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSAnd the servants of Amon conspired against him, and slew the king in his own house.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd the people of the land slew all them that had conspired against king Amon; and the people of the land made Josiah his son king in his stead.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxNow the rest of the acts of Amon which he did, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbAnd he was buried in his sepulchre in the garden of Uzza: and Josiah his son reigned in his stead.¦layout ªlast_verse